&#x27;MARSHAL IS NO MORE&#x27;

&#x27;The Shogunate&#x27;s liaison council announced at six o&#x27;clock today the passing of His Highness Moriuji Ashikaga, Senior Third Rank, Lord General of the Six Guards.&#x27;

&#x27;Regarding the date and time of passing, the cause of death and so on, not one word of explanation has been given. It has only been conveyed that His Highness Shirou Kuniuji, eldest grandson of the late Lord General, will enter the main keep of Fudaraku Castle and is scheduled to carry out the work of government in his place.&#x27;

&#x27;In the whirl of confusion every circle has its own rumor flying: conspiracy from Kyoto, secret moves by the occupation forces, revenge by Okabe remnants, and so on and so on. Some are also linking it with the closure of Hachimangu in force since the recent sacred-sword offering pilgrimage, but&#x27;

&#x27;not one theory has evidence to its name. All remain within the realm of speculation.&#x27;

&#x27;However, as per informed sources, the Lord General&#x27;s good health was beyond all doubt. If this is correct, death by illness is unthinkable, and it appears that some human hand was involved in the passing.&#x27;

